\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Fling out the banner! Let it float
\par Skyward and seaward, high and wide;
\par The sun shall light its shining folds,
\par The Cross on which the Saviour died.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fling out the banner! Angels bend
\par In anxious silence o'er the sign;
\par And vainly seek to comprehend
\par The wonder of the Love Divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fling out the banner! Heathen lands
\par Shall see from far the glorious sight,
\par And nations, crowding to be born,
\par Baptize their spirits in its light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fling out the banner! Let it float
\par Skyward and seaward, high and wide,
\par Our glory, only in the Cross;
\par Our only hope, the crucified!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Fling out the banner! Wide and high,
\par Seaward and skyward, let it shine;
\par Nor skill, nor might, nor merit ours:
\par We conquer only in that sign. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

